{"key": "0059d18b5645896968704ebf056dd51a", "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "response": {"content": [{"text": "I can't confirm any ticket has been opened. A ticket for terminal T1988B can only be proposed, and nothing runs until you confirm; an unconfirmed proposal expires after 15 minutes [policy:capabilities]. The reason options for the ticket are \"no connection\", \"no signal\" or \"transaction error\" [policy:capabilities].\n\nSteps to try first, based on the sources:\n1. Check the chip: with the terminal off, open the back cover and insert the chip in the slot marked SIM1 or SIM2, metal side down. Close the cover, turn the terminal on and wait for the data network connection. When it shows a connected network (2G or 3G), it is ready to use [3].\n2. Run a communication test: press the function button (F, # or your terminal's own), select option 2 – maintenance, then option 1 – communication test [6].\n3. If the error is ADQ 1-84 (signal fluctuation), press Function, enter 25 (the screen turns green), enter the Operator Password, select Function 46, then make a test sale [2].\n4. If the error is ADQ 1-87 (chip registration), confirm the chip is properly inserted, then press Function, enter 25, enter the Merchant Password, select Function 46, then Function 90 (the screen turns green after each step), and make a test sale [1].\n\nThe sources do not say which steps apply to the T1988B model specifically.\n\nMISSING: steps specific to model T1988B", "type": "text"}], "id": "msg_011CgifZbPnPxUFCFHDAJVEo", "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 3005, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 4126, "output_tokens": 465, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}}, "role": "agent", "scope": "approval-04#0"}
